  {
    "type": "math_show",
    "q": "Restrict the appropriate domain of $y=\\tan x$ to be one-to-one function.",
    "c": "<strong>အဖြေရှင်းလင်းချက်:</strong><br><br>The tangent function $y = \\tan x$ is periodic with a period of $\\pi$.<br><br>To make it a one-to-one function, we must restrict its domain to a single continuous branch between its vertical asymptotes.<br><br>The vertical asymptotes of $y = \\tan x$ occur at $x = -\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ and $x = \\frac{\\pi}{2}$.<br><br>Therefore, the appropriate restricted domain is:<br><br>$$-\\frac{\\pi}{2} < x < \\frac{\\pi}{2}$$<br><br><strong>$-\\frac{\\pi}{2} < x < \\frac{\\pi}{2}$</strong>"
  },
  {
    "type": "math_show",
    "q": "Find the value of $\\csc\\left[ \\tan^{-1}\\left\\{ \\frac{1}{2}\\sec\\left( 2\\sin^{-1}\\frac{1}{2} \\right) \\right\\} \\right]$.",
    "c": "<strong>အဖြေရှင်းလင်းချက်:</strong><br><br>First, evaluate the innermost inverse trigonometric function:<br><br>$$\\sin^{-1}\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) = \\frac{\\pi}{6}$$<br><br>Multiply by $2$:<br><br>$$2\\sin^{-1}\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) = 2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right) = \\frac{\\pi}{3}$$<br><br>Next, evaluate the secant function:<br><br>$$\\sec\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right) = \\frac{1}{\\cos(\\pi/3)} = \\frac{1}{1/2} = 2$$<br><br>Multiply by $\\frac{1}{2}$:<br><br>$$\\frac{1}{2}\\sec\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right) = \\frac{1}{2}(2) = 1$$<br><br>Next, evaluate the inverse tangent:<br><br>$$\\tan^{-1}(1) = \\frac{\\pi}{4}$$<br><br>Finally, evaluate the cosecant function:<br><br>$$\\csc\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right) = \\frac{1}{\\sin(\\pi/4)} = \\frac{1}{1/\\sqrt{2}} = \\sqrt{2}$$<br><br><strong>$\\sqrt{2}$</strong>"
  },
  {
    "type": "math_show",
    "q": "Restrict the appropriate domain of $y=\\sin x$ to be a one-to-one function.",
    "c": "<strong>အဖြေရှင်းလင်းချက်:</strong><br><br>The sine function $y = \\sin x$ is periodic and not one-to-one over its entire domain.<br><br>To define its inverse function, we must restrict its domain to an interval where it is strictly increasing and covers the full range $[-1, 1]$.<br><br>The standard principal branch for the sine function is from $-\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ to $\\frac{\\pi}{2}$.<br><br>Therefore, the restricted domain is:<br><br>$$-\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\le x \\le \\frac{\\pi}{2}$$<br><br><strong>$-\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\le x \\le \\frac{\\pi}{2}$</strong>"
  },
  {
    "type": "math_show",
    "q": "Find a and b such that a and b are amplitude and period of the graph of $y=4\\cos 3x+7$.",
    "c": "<strong>အဖြေရှင်းလင်းချက်:</strong><br><br>The general form of the cosine function is $y = A\\cos(Bx) + C$.<br><br>For the given function $y = 4\\cos 3x + 7$, we have $A = 4$, $B = 3$, and $C = 7$.<br><br>The amplitude $a$ is the absolute value of $A$:<br><br>$$a = |4| = 4$$<br><br>The period $b$ is given by the formula $\\frac{2\\pi}{|B|}$:<br><br>$$b = \\frac{2\\pi}{3}$$<br><br><strong>$a=4, b=\\frac{2\\pi}{3}$</strong>"
  },
  {
    "type": "math_show",
    "q": "Restrict the appropriate domain of $y=\\sin x$ to define the inverse function.",
    "c": "<strong>အဖြေရှင်းလင်းချက်:</strong><br><br>To define the inverse sine function $y = \\sin^{-1}x$, the domain of the original sine function $y = \\sin x$ must be restricted.<br><br>This restriction ensures the function is one-to-one and its range remains $[-1, 1]$.<br><br>The standard restricted domain for the sine function is the interval:<br><br>$$-\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\le x \\le \\frac{\\pi}{2}$$<br><br><strong>$-\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\le x \\le \\frac{\\pi}{2}$</strong>"
  },
  {
    "type": "math_show",
    "q": "Evaluate $\\cos^{-1}\\left( \\cos\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right) \\right)$.",
    "c": "<strong>အဖြေရှင်းလင်းချက်:</strong><br><br>The identity $\\cos^{-1}(\\cos \\theta) = \\theta$ holds true if and only if $0 \\le \\theta \\le \\pi$.<br><br>Here, $\\theta = -\\frac{1}{2}$, which is not in the interval $[0, \\pi]$.<br><br>However, the cosine function is an even function, meaning $\\cos(-\\theta) = \\cos(\\theta)$.<br><br>Therefore, we can write:<br><br>$$\\cos\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right) = \\cos\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)$$<br><br>Since $\\frac{1}{2}$ is within the principal range $[0, \\pi]$, we have:<br><br><div style='overflow-x: auto; max-width: 100%; white-space: nowrap;'>$$\\cos^{-1}\\left( \\cos\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right) \\right) <br><br>= \\cos^{-1}\\left( \\cos\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) \\right)$$</div><br><br>$$= \\frac{1}{2}$$<br><br><strong>$\\frac{1}{2}$</strong>"
  },
  {
    "type": "math_show",
    "q": "Find the value of $\\sin^{-1}(\\cos^{-1}(\\cos 0.2)) + \\sin^{-1}(-0.2) + \\cos^{-1}(\\sin^{-1}(\\sin 0.2)) + \\cos^{-1}(-0.2)$.",
    "c": "<strong>အဖြေရှင်းလင်းချက်:</strong><br><br>First, simplify $\\cos^{-1}(\\cos 0.2)$. Since $0 \\le 0.2 \\le \\pi$, we have:<br><br>$$\\cos^{-1}(\\cos 0.2) = 0.2$$<br><br>So the first two terms become:<br><br>$$\\sin^{-1}(0.2) + \\sin^{-1}(-0.2)$$<br><br>Since $\\sin^{-1}(-x) = -\\sin^{-1}(x)$, these two terms cancel out to $0$.<br><br>Next, simplify $\\sin^{-1}(\\sin 0.2)$. Since $-\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\le 0.2 \\le \\frac{\\pi}{2}$, we have:<br><br>$$\\sin^{-1}(\\sin 0.2) = 0.2$$<br><br>The last two terms become:<br><br>$$\\cos^{-1}(0.2) + \\cos^{-1}(-0.2)$$<br><br>Using the identity $\\cos^{-1}(x) + \\cos^{-1}(-x) = \\pi$, we get:<br><br>$$\\cos^{-1}(0.2) + \\cos^{-1}(-0.2) = \\pi$$<br><br>Adding all parts together:<br><br>$$0 + \\pi = \\pi$$<br><br><strong>$\\pi$</strong>"
  },
  {
    "type": "math_show",
    "q": "If a and b are the period and amplitude of the graph of $y=\\cos x$, then find the sum of a and b.",
    "c": "<strong>အဖြေရှင်းလင်းချက်:</strong><br><br>For the basic cosine function $y = \\cos x$, the amplitude $b$ is $1$.<br><br>The period $a$ of the basic cosine function is $2\\pi$.<br><br>We are asked to find the sum of the period $a$ and the amplitude $b$.<br><br>$$a + b = 2\\pi + 1$$<br><br><strong>$2\\pi+1$</strong>"
  },
  {
    "type": "math_show",
    "q": "Find c+d if c and d are amplitude and period of the graph of $y=3\\sin 2x+1$ respectively.",
    "c": "<strong>အဖြေရှင်းလင်းချက်:</strong><br><br>For the function $y = 3\\sin 2x + 1$, the amplitude $c$ is the coefficient of the sine function:<br><br>$$c = 3$$<br><br>The period $d$ is calculated using the formula $\\frac{2\\pi}{|B|}$, where $B = 2$:<br><br>$$d = \\frac{2\\pi}{2} = \\pi$$<br><br>We need to find the sum $c + d$:<br><br>$$c + d = 3 + \\pi$$<br><br><strong>$3+\\pi$</strong>"
  },
  {
    "type": "math_show",
    "q": "Evaluate the value of $\\sin\\left( \\tan^{-1}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\right)$.",
    "c": "<strong>အဖြေရှင်းလင်းချက်:</strong><br><br>Let $\\theta = \\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\right)$.<br><br>This means $\\tan \\theta = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$.<br><br>Since the range of $\\tan^{-1}$ is $\\left(-\\frac{\\pi}{2}, \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)$, the angle is:<br><br>$$\\theta = \\frac{\\pi}{6}$$<br><br>We need to evaluate $\\sin \\theta$:<br><br>$$\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right) = \\frac{1}{2}$$<br><br><strong>$\\frac{1}{2}$</strong>"
  },
  {
    "type": "math_show",
    "q": "What is the amplitude of a periodic function ?",
    "c": "<strong>အဖြေရှင်းလင်းချက်:</strong><br><br>The amplitude of a periodic function is defined as half the difference between its maximum and minimum values.<br><br>This can be expressed with the formula:<br><br>$$\\text{amplitude} = \\frac{\\max - \\min}{2}$$<br><br><strong>$\\text{amplitude} = \\frac{\\max - \\min}{2}$</strong>"
  },
  {
    "type": "math_show",
    "q": "Find p+q given the following graph of the function $y=\\tan px+q$.<br><div style='width: 300px; height: 300px; margin: 20px auto; border: 1px solid #444; padding: 10px; background: #1e1e1e; border-radius: 8px;'><svg viewBox='0 0 400 400' width='100%' height='100%' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'><line x1='0' y1='200' x2='400' y2='200' stroke='#FFFFFF' stroke-width='2'/><line x1='200' y1='0' x2='200' y2='400' stroke='#FFFFFF' stroke-width='2'/><path d='M 90 350 C 105 200, 110 160, 120 160 C 130 160, 135 120, 150 50 M 170 350 C 185 200, 190 160, 200 160 C 210 160, 215 120, 230 50 M 250 350 C 265 200, 270 160, 280 160 C 290 160, 295 120, 310 50' fill='none' stroke='#00EEFF' stroke-width='4'/> <line x1='160' y1='0' x2='160' y2='400' stroke='#888' stroke-width='1' stroke-dasharray='5,5'/> <line x1='240' y1='0' x2='240' y2='400' stroke='#888' stroke-width='1' stroke-dasharray='5,5'/> <line x1='320' y1='0' x2='320' y2='400' stroke='#888' stroke-width='1' stroke-dasharray='5,5'/> <line x1='80' y1='0' x2='80' y2='400' stroke='#888' stroke-width='1' stroke-dasharray='5,5'/> <line x1='0' y1='160' x2='400' y2='160' stroke='#888' stroke-width='1' stroke-dasharray='5,5'/> <text x='70' y='215' fill='white' font-size='12'>-3π</text> <text x='110' y='215' fill='white' font-size='12'>-2π</text> <text x='150' y='215' fill='white' font-size='12'>-π</text> <text x='190' y='215' fill='white' font-size='12'>0</text> <text x='235' y='215' fill='white' font-size='12'>π</text> <text x='270' y='215' fill='white' font-size='12'>2π</text> <text x='310' y='215' fill='white' font-size='12'>3π</text> <text x='190' y='155' fill='white' font-size='12'>1</text> <text x='385' y='215' fill='white' font-size='14'>x</text> <text x='205' y='15' fill='white' font-size='14'>y</text> </svg></div>",
    "c": "<strong>အဖြေရှင်းလင်းချက်:</strong><br><br>From the graph, the function passes through the y-intercept $(0, 1)$.<br><br>Substitute $x = 0$ and $y = 1$ into $y = \\tan(px) + q$:<br><br><div class=\"math-line\">\\(1 = \\tan(0) + q\\)</div><div class=\"math-line\">\\(\\implies q = 1\\)</div><br><br>The vertical asymptotes are shown at $x = -\\pi$ and $x = \\pi$.<br><br>The period is the distance between consecutive asymptotes:<br><br>$$\\text{Period} = \\pi - (-\\pi) = 2\\pi$$<br><br>The period of $y = \\tan(px)$ is given by $\\frac{\\pi}{|p|}$.<br><br><div class=\"math-line\">\\(\\frac{\\pi}{p} = 2\\pi\\)</div><div class=\"math-line\">\\(\\implies p = \\frac{1}{2}\\)</div><br><br>Finally, find the sum $p + q$:<br><br>$$p + q = \\frac{1}{2} + 1 = \\frac{3}{2}$$<br><br><strong>$\\frac{3}{2}$</strong><br><svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 330\" width=\"100%\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Tangent graph with the marked asymptotes\" data-chapter-graph=\"1\"><rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" fill=\"#1e1e1e\"/><defs><clipPath id=\"cg366\"><rect x=\"50\" y=\"30\" width=\"386\" height=\"258\"/></clipPath></defs><line x1=\"139.2\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"139.2\" y2=\"288\" stroke=\"#2A3548\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"346.8\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"346.8\" y2=\"288\" stroke=\"#2A3548\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"50\" y1=\"276.3\" x2=\"436\" y2=\"276.3\" stroke=\"#2A3548\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"50\" y1=\"227.4\" x2=\"436\" y2=\"227.4\" stroke=\"#2A3548\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"50\" y1=\"129.7\" x2=\"436\" y2=\"129.7\" stroke=\"#2A3548\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"50\" y1=\"80.8\" x2=\"436\" y2=\"80.8\" stroke=\"#2A3548\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"50\" y1=\"178.5\" x2=\"436\" y2=\"178.5\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><polygon points=\"436,178.5 428,174.5 428,182.5\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/><text x=\"434\" y=\"170.5\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"end\">x</text><line x1=\"243.0\" y1=\"288\" x2=\"243.0\" y2=