288\" stroke=\"#94A3B8\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-dasharray=\"6,4\"/><line x1=\"294.9\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"294.9\" y2=\"288\" stroke=\"#94A3B8\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-dasharray=\"6,4\"/><line x1=\"398.6\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"398.6\" y2=\"288\" stroke=\"#94A3B8\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-dasharray=\"6,4\"/><line x1=\"50\" y1=\"159.0\" x2=\"436\" y2=\"159.0\" stroke=\"#94A3B8\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-dasharray=\"6,4\"/></g><text x=\"87.4\" y=\"44.0\" fill=\"#F0B90B\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\">x = -3π</text><text x=\"191.1\" y=\"44.0\" fill=\"#F0B90B\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\">x = -π</text><text x=\"294.9\" y=\"44.0\" fill=\"#F0B90B\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\">x = π</text><text x=\"398.6\" y=\"44.0\" fill=\"#F0B90B\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\">x = 3π</text><text x=\"432.0\" y=\"155.0\" fill=\"#F0B90B\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"end\">y = 1</text><circle cx=\"243.0\" cy=\"159.0\" r=\"4.2\" fill=\"#F0B90B\" stroke=\"#1e1e1e\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"251.0\" y=\"153.0\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"start\">(0, 1)</text></svg>"
  },
  {
    "type": "math_show",
    "q": "Find the sum of amplitude and period of the graph of $y=3\\cos\\frac{\\pi}{4}x$.",
    "c": "<strong>အဖြေရှင်းလင်းချက်:</strong><br><br>For the function $y = 3\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}x\\right)$, the amplitude is the absolute value of the coefficient:<br><br>$$\\text{Amplitude} = 3$$<br><br>The period is calculated using the formula $\\frac{2\\pi}{|B|}$, where $B = \\frac{\\pi}{4}$:<br><br>$$\\text{Period} = \\frac{2\\pi}{\\pi/4} = 2\\pi \\times \\frac{4}{\\pi} = 8$$<br><br>The sum of the amplitude and period is:<br><br>$$3 + 8 = 11$$<br><br><strong>$11$</strong>"
  },
  {
    "type": "math_show",
    "q": "Find the amplitude and period of the graph $y=4\\cos 3x+7$.",
    "c": "<strong>အဖြေရှင်းလင်းချက်:</strong><br><br>For the function $y = 4\\cos 3x + 7$, the amplitude is the absolute value of the coefficient of the cosine term:<br><br>$$\\text{Amplitude} = 4$$<br><br>The period is calculated using the formula $\\frac{2\\pi}{|B|}$, where $B = 3$:<br><br>$$\\text{Period} = \\frac{2\\pi}{3}$$<br><br><strong>$\\text{Amplitude: } 4 \\text{ , Period: } \\frac{2\\pi}{3}$</strong>"
  },
  {
    "type": "math_show",
    "q": "If a and b are the period and amplitude of the graph of $y=\\sin x$, then find the sum of a and b.",
    "c": "<strong>အဖြေရှင်းလင်းချက်:</strong><br><br>For the basic sine function $y = \\sin x$, the period $a$ is $2\\pi$.<br><br>The amplitude $b$ is $1$.<br><br>We are asked to find the sum of the period $a$ and the amplitude $b$.<br><br>$$a + b = 2\\pi + 1$$<br><br><strong>$2\\pi+1$</strong>"
  },
  {
    "type": "math_show",
    "q": "Find the value of $\\tan^{-1}\\left( 2\\cos\\left( 2\\sin^{-1}\\frac{1}{2} \\right) \\right)$.",
    "c": "<strong>အဖြေရှင်းလင်းချက်:</strong><br><br>First, evaluate the innermost inverse trigonometric function:<br><br>$$\\sin^{-1}\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) = \\frac{\\pi}{6}$$<br><br>Multiply by $2$:<br><br>$$2\\sin^{-1}\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) = 2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right) = \\frac{\\pi}{3}$$<br><br>Next, evaluate the cosine function:<br><br>$$\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right) = \\frac{1}{2}$$<br><br>Multiply by $2$:<br><br>$$2\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right) = 2\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) = 1$$<br><br>Finally, evaluate the inverse tangent:<br><br>$$\\tan^{-1}(1) = \\frac{\\pi}{4}$$<br><br><strong>$\\frac{\\pi}{4}$</strong>"
  },
  {
    "type": "math_show",
    "q": "Find the value of $\\sin^{-1}\\left( \\cos\\left( \\sin^{-1}\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\right) \\right)$.",
    "c": "<strong>အဖြေရှင်းလင်းချက်:</strong><br><br>First, evaluate the innermost inverse trigonometric function:<br><br>$$\\sin^{-1}\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right) = \\frac{\\pi}{3}$$<br><br>Next, evaluate the cosine function:<br><br>$$\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right) = \\frac{1}{2}$$<br><br>Finally, evaluate the inverse sine function:<br><br>$$\\sin^{-1}\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) = \\frac{\\pi}{6}$$<br><br><strong>$\\frac{\\pi}{6}$</strong>"
  }
]
